Poseidon for AmigaOS @POSEIDON_PKG_VERSION@
========================

The Poseidon USB stack for AmigaOS 3.1 and newer, with the Trident preferences
editor and the full set of USB device classes.

Every component in this archive reports the same version.
The classes and tools require poseidon.library 6 or newer.


REQUIREMENTS
------------

Kickstart and Workbench 3.1 or newer, a 68020 or better, and MUI 3.8 or newer
for Trident and the per-class settings windows (the stack itself runs without
MUI). You also need a USB host-controller driver - none ships here.

The Install script needs Installer 43.3 or newer, which is freely
distributable and is on Aminet as util/misc/Installer-43_3.lha. OS 3.5 and
later already have one; a stock 3.1 install disk does not.

Below OS 3.2 a held key on a USB keyboard does not auto-repeat, and below
workbench.library 45 USBEject's eject entries sit flat in the Tools menu
rather than under their own USB title. See the README for the full list.


CPU VARIANT
-----------

  @M68K_CPU@
  @CPU_DESCRIPTION@

Three archives are released, one per CPU - -020, -040 and -060. Take the one
that matches your machine.

No variant needs an FPU. The stack itself - poseidon.library, the classes,
Trident and USBEject - contains no floating point at all. The only floating
point in the distribution is the gamma table computed by the two optional
camera tools, PencamTool and SonixcamTool; in the -020 archive that is
soft-float, and in the -040/-060 archives 68040.library/68060.library cover
it on a part without an FPU.

Every component here reports its CPU in its version string, so you can always
check what is installed:

  Version LIBS:poseidon.library
  -> poseidon.library @POSEIDON_PKG_VERSION@ (...) Poseidon for AmigaOS @M68K_CPU@


BUILD VARIANT
-------------

  @DEBUG_BACKEND@
  @DEBUG_BACKEND_DESCRIPTION@

The 'off' archive is the normal download. The 'serial' archive is identical
except the stack, classes and tools also emit debug output, for
troubleshooting.


INSTALLATION
------------

  Double-click the Install icon, or run `Installer Install` from a Shell,
  and follow the prompts. A reboot is recommended afterwards so the freshly
  installed poseidon.library and USB classes are picked up.

SWITCHING CPU VARIANT
---------------------

  All three CPU archives carry the same version number - that number is the
  library's ABI version, not the build variant - so installing one over
  another is a same-version copy, and the Installer's version check would
  otherwise skip it. Run the Installer at the Average or Expert user level,
  where it shows the version requester and lets you overwrite, or delete the
  previously installed files first.
